# Build context for .devcontainer/Dockerfile only (BuildKit reads
# <Dockerfile>.dockerignore in preference to the root .dockerignore, which
# belongs to the production image and is left alone).
#
# An allowlist: the image needs the two requirements files and nothing else —
# the source is bind-mounted at run time. This keeps .git, .venv, data/,
# node_modules and any .env out of the context, and
# keeps the context a few kilobytes regardless of what the checkout holds.
*
!requirements.txt
!requirements-dev.txt
